Here are the two exact fixes you need.
The reason the data is "overriding" the headers when you scroll is because your header background color is currently set to alpha(theme.palette.primary.main, 0.08). The alpha makes it **transparent**, meaning you can see the text scrolling underneath it! We will change it to a solid color.
We will also completely remove the Journal ID grouping from the table.
### 1. Fix the Scrolling Overlap (Update Styles)
Find the styles object at the top of your file. We need to change the tableHeaderCell to have a solid background color so scrolling rows hide behind it properly.
**Find this block (around line 47):**
```javascript
  tableHeaderCell: {
    fontWeight: "bold",
    backgroundColor: (theme) => alpha(theme.palette.primary.main, 0.08),
    whiteSpace: "nowrap",
    zIndex: 10,
  },

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
  tableHeaderCell: {
    fontWeight: "bold",
    backgroundColor: "#f5f6f8", // FIX: Solid light-grey background so text doesn't show through!
    color: "text.primary",
    whiteSpace: "nowrap",
    zIndex: 10,
  },

```
*(Note: You can also safely delete stickyHeaderColumn and stickyBodyColumn from the styles object since we are removing the Journal ID column completely).*
### 2. Remove "Journal ID" from the Table
Scroll down to your View Details modal's <DialogContent> (around line 550). We are removing the Journal ID header and the grouped rendering logic.
**Replace your entire <TableHead> and <TableBody> with this:**
```javascript
                    <TableHead>
                      <TableRow>
                        <TableCell align="center" sx={styles.tableHeaderCell}>Branch</TableCell>
                        <TableCell align="center" sx={styles.tableHeaderCell}>Currency</TableCell>
                        <TableCell align="center" sx={styles.tableHeaderCell}>CGL</TableCell>
                        <TableCell align="center" sx={styles.tableHeaderCell}>Amount</TableCell>
                        <TableCell align="center" sx={styles.tableHeaderCell}>Type</TableCell>
                      </TableRow>
                    </TableHead>
                    <TableBody>
                      {batchDetails.map((group) => {
                        return group.map((row) => (
                          <TableRow key={row.id} hover>
                            <TableCell align="center">{row.branch}</TableCell>
                            <TableCell align="center">{row.currency}</TableCell>
                            <TableCell align="center">{row.cgl}</TableCell>
                            <TableCell align="center">{formatCurrency(row.amount)}</TableCell>
                            <TableCell align="center">
                              <Chip label={row.transactionType} color={getTxnTypeColor(row.transactionType)} size="small" />
                            </TableCell>
                          </TableRow>
                        ));
                      })}
                    </TableBody>

```
That's it!
 1. The table will now correctly show exactly the 5 columns you requested.
 2. The sticky header will remain firmly locked at the top as you scroll, and the solid background will hide the rows sliding underneath it!
